{
  "name": "libfringe",
  "description": "libfringe is a low-level Rust library for implementing high-performance, lightweight context switches and green threading without kernel intervention. It provides architecture-specific assembly for x86 and x86_64 to achieve sub-10ns swap times while supporting both hosted and bare-metal (no_std) environments. The library exposes safe generator abstractions alongside unsafe primitives for manual stack management, guard page allocation, and context manipulation.",
